<Diagram caption={"The same two images in three places. Only the proxy, where PostgreSQL and the bucket live, and how you run one-off commands change."}>
<svg viewBox="0 0 960 450" role="img" aria-labelledby="topo-t topo-d" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
<title id="topo-t">Deployment topology for Docker, Fly.io and Portainer</title>
<desc id="topo-d">In all three setups a TLS-terminating proxy fronts the gateway and the admin console, both run the same published images on port 8080, the gateway uses PostgreSQL and an S3-compatible bucket, and the admin console uses a separate database on the PostgreSQL server.</desc>
<defs>
<marker id="topo-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="arrow-fill"/></marker>
<marker id="topo-ac" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="arrow-accent"/></marker>
</defs>
